{"main_ref":{"ref":"refs/heads/tb371fc","node_id":"REF_kwDOV4BGPrJyZWZzL2hlYWRzL3RiMzcxZmM","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/git/refs/heads/tb371fc","object":{"sha":"8d0bc64d8da6da18bf43b52a2a9547f28f44c3e9","type":"commit","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/git/commits/8d0bc64d8da6da18bf43b52a2a9547f28f44c3e9"}},"pr":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pulls/36","id":5483916509,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BGPs8AAAABRt3s3Q","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pull/36","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pull/36.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pull/36.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/issues/36","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pulls/36/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pulls/36/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/issues/36/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/statuses/66d9e20a9541b503ed4f5cac5c79c8a5b4a0809b","number":36,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"hw/misc: add verified SM8250 RPM statistics offset reference","user":{"login":"cyjin-yl","id":19223209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIzMjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19223209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why this is needed\n\nThe qualified SPSS build `54ec7443bc75460baa35a0c0b0502ae6cb4d8fa7` reached an original Android kernel fault in `msm_rpmstats_probe+0x84`: a 32-bit read at `0x0c3f0004`. That native attempt used the unchanged backed-up kernel, ramdisk, full DT and bootargs, with zero LUNs because the reviewed complete-media ready file was absent. It ended in kernel failure; Android userspace, UI and boot completion remain unobserved.\n\nThis change addresses that exact offset-word access. The base is merged SPSS commit `8d0bc64d8da6da18bf43b52a2a9547f28f44c3e9`; it preserves the other lane's separately published SPSS evidence.\n\n## Resulting behavior\n\n- Add `qcom-sm8250-rpm-stats-offset`, default disabled. The reference profile maps exactly four bytes at `0x0c3f0004`.\n- An enabled, aligned 32-bit read returns `0x000f0048`. All writes, disabled accesses, narrow/unaligned/typed 64-bit reads and neighboring holes are rejected.\n- Raw five-byte reads validate only the successful four-byte prefix and independently require rejection of the neighboring byte. Failed suffix values are not interpreted.\n- No statistics records, counters, names, DDR-offset word, firmware behavior, READY state, IRQ, clock or timer are synthesized. The existing AOP mailbox mapping is unchanged.\n- Expose 17 pure QOM observations. VMState v1 is exactly 24 bytes; loading strictly validates target profile, RSO1 identity, geometry and profile-specific offset, without repair.\n\n## Source evidence\n\nThe generator pins complete bytes for four public files before parsing: vendor `rpm_stats.c` and `kona-pm.dtsi` at OnePlus commit `98719830b0de5584f5588bbe9f4c8304d97a64c6`, and upstream `qcom_stats.c` and `sm8250.dtsi` at Linux commit `adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a`. It derives `0x0c3f0000 + 0x48 - 0x0c300000 = 0x000f0048` and regenerates two exact outputs.\n\nThe original full DT and the 456-byte original kernel probe independently establish the address and consumer behavior. Static inspection of the existing backed-up AOP firmware corroborates the producer arithmetic. This is not proof of firmware execution, reset reachability, a general address alias, a live hardware value, or immutable physical SRAM. Only bounded derived evidence is included; no private firmware image is published.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Independent static implementation and test reviews passed.\n- Four complete pinned public inputs reproduced both generated outputs byte-for-byte.\n- Four whole-input identity mutations, 22 parser negative vectors, a bad complete transport response and two output mutations were rejected.\n- Add 20 compiled device groups: ordinary boundary semantics, default-off, paused TCG, two completed migrations, two profile mismatch directions and six one-bit corrupted streams. Validate full 24-byte wire payloads, two original/eight total stream files, and two 17-getter target snapshots before any restored-state memory access or `cont`.\n- Migration targets prewarm RAM witnesses only; the immutable device is not described as dirtied.\n- The CI plan is now 97 component gates plus five Linux diagnostics. All earlier 100 contracts and their order are unchanged. The harness unit suite contains 35 tests.\n\nLocal unit verification is recorded accurately: an initial isolated import invocation failed before collecting tests; the corrected CI-style import invocation ran 35 tests, with 34 passing and one existing socket fixture blocked by this environment's AF_UNIX permission restriction. Neither was reported as a complete pass. Formal CI must pass all 35.\n\n**This is a draft pending actual compiled CI, independent artifact/log auditing and a separately bound native attempt. No native execution or Android success is claimed for this head.**\n\n## Actual CI correction\n\nThe first published head `75cc1dc83600784afa06e81c9998d8d39aba6af2` failed the push board build because the new header referenced `hw/sysbus.h`. The current repository uses `hw/core/sysbus.h`. Follow-up head `66d9e20a9541b503ed4f5cac5c79c8a5b4a0809b` corrects exactly that include and adds the failed-build and independent correction receipts. C behavior, generated data, test bytes and CI requirements are unchanged. The original static review and failed build remain recorded; neither establishes compilability.\n\nFresh attempt-1 push run [45533031476](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45533031476) and PR run [45533037101](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45533037101) are in progress for the corrected source. The draft remains unqualified pending their actual results and artifact audit.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T02:22:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T02:29:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c7ba198d6bf9bd5e3255e207d07efd85a026a1a9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"cyjin-yl:tb371fc-verified-rpm-stats-offset-20261125-6a5","ref":"tb371fc-verified-rpm-stats-offset-20261125-6a5","repo":{"id":1468024382,"node_id":"R_kgDOV4BGPg","name":"qemu-tb371fc","full_name":"cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc","owner":{"login":"cyjin-yl","id":19223209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjIzMjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19223209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl","html_url":"https://github.com/cyjin-yl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-yl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyjin-